---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// /roadmap/: where the project is, what exists, what merged since Phase 0, what is measured, and what comes after 1.0.
// Facts: docs/content-inventory.md sections 3.11, 9 and 10 (state as of product HEAD 7728d7c, 2026-11-23).
// Built is not the same as usable: nothing here can import, play or export real video yet.
import '../../styles/area-s3.css';
import '../../styles/area-progress.css';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Section from '../../components/ui/Section.astro';
import Card from '../../components/ui/Card.astro';
import StatusChip from '../../components/ui/StatusChip.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
import RoadmapTimeline from '../../components/roadmap/RoadmapTimeline.astro';
import RecentlyMerged from '../../components/roadmap/RecentlyMerged.astro';
import ProofStrip from '../../components/roadmap/ProofStrip.astro';
import { BUILT, NEXT_IN_P1, AFTER_1_0, AS_OF } from '../../data/roadmap';
import { LINKS } from '../../site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Where Cutweave is"
  description="The Cutweave roadmap: Phase 0 is done, Phase 1 is 40 of 60 work packages in, and there is no download yet. What is built, what merged since Phase 0, what is measured, and what comes after 1.0."
>
  <header class="hero">
    <Container>
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Roadmap</p>
        <h1>Where Cutweave is</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Phase 0 is done with a provisional go. Phase 1 is {AS_OF.p1Done} of {AS_OF.p1Total} work packages in, and there is no download yet.
        </p>
        <p class="stamp">
          <StatusChip status="in-progress" label="Pre-alpha · Phase 1 of 7" />
          <span>As of <time datetime={AS_OF.iso}>{AS_OF.label}</time>. Dates are rough and are re-estimated after each phase.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          Built is not the same as usable. The engine, the agent interface and the first editor panels exist and are
          tested, but nothing can import, play or export a real video yet: that waits on the FFmpeg backend.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </header>

  <Section id="phases" eyebrow="The plan" title="Eight phases to 1.0" lede="Each phase ends at a milestone with a test you can check. The marigold marker shows the phase being worked on now.">
    <RoadmapTimeline />
    <p class="plan-note">
      The plan is about 14 months to 1.0 and about 7.5 months to a Public Alpha. Human review capacity is the stated
      bottleneck.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="built" tone="raised" eyebrow="In the repo today" title="What exists" lede="This is code that runs in tests. Each card says what it is attached to, because most of it is not something you can use yet.">
    <ul class="cards">
      {BUILT.map((b) => (
        <Card as="li">
          <div><StatusChip status="built" {...(b.chip ? { label: b.chip } : {})} /></div>
          <h3 class="card-title">{b.title}</h3>
          <p class="card-text">{b.text}</p>
        </Card>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section id="recent" eyebrow="Built since Phase 0" title={`${AS_OF.recentlyMerged} work packages in two days`} lede="Merged to the main branch on 22 and 23 November 2026, newest first. Most of it is written by AI coding agents from public work packages, under human review. The hash links to the merge commit.">
    <RecentlyMerged headingLevel={3} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="next" tone="raised" eyebrow="Still to merge" title="What is left in Phase 1" lede={`${AS_OF.p1Total - AS_OF.p1Done} of ${AS_OF.p1Total} work packages. Together they make up the M1 milestone: an agent and the interface both import, cut and export.`}>
    <ul class="cards">
      {NEXT_IN_P1.map((n) => (
        <Card as="li">
          <div><StatusChip status="planned" label={n.blocked ? 'Blocked on FFmpeg' : 'Planned · P1'} /></div>
          <h3 class="card-title">{n.title}</h3>
          <p class="card-text">{n.text}</p>
          <p class="card-wps">{n.wps}</p>
        </Card>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="plan-note">
      While the FFmpeg spike (S3) is blocked, the work that does not need it goes ahead against stand-ins: a stub media
      backend for dev builds, generated audio and synthetic frames. These do not replace the M1 exit, which needs real
      media.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="proof" eyebrow="Evidence" title="Measured so far" lede="Numbers from tests in the real code, and from the throwaway Phase 0 prototypes that tested the riskiest ideas first. Each group carries its own label.">
    <ProofStrip variant="full" headingLevel={3} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="after" tone="raised" eyebrow="Beyond the plan" title="After 1.0" lede="In rough order. None of this is promised for 1.0.">
    <ol class="later">
      {AFTER_1_0.map((item) => (
        <li><StatusChip status="later" /> <span>{item}</span></li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section id="follow" width="narrow" eyebrow="Keep up" title="How to follow along" lede="The work happens in public on GitHub. There is no newsletter, and nothing to sign up for.">
    <ul class="follow">
      <li><a href={LINKS.repo}>The repository</a>: the code and its history.</li>
      <li><a href={LINKS.issues}>Issues</a>: work packages, bugs and requests.</li>
      <li><a href={LINKS.docs}>The docs folder</a>: the product brief, architecture, roadmap and decision records.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="actions">
      <Button href={LINKS.repo} variant="primary" external icon="github">Follow on GitHub</Button>
      <Button href="/open-source/" iconEnd="arrow-right">See how to contribute</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: var(--section-space) var(--space-8); background: var(--glow-marigold); }
  .hero-inner { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--stack-md); max-width: var(--prose-max); }
  .eyebrow { font-size: var(--s3-text-xs); line-height: var(--s3-text-xs-line); font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: var(--eyebrow-tracking); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--display-hero-size); line-height: var(--display-hero-line); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--text-lede-size); line-height: var(--text-lede-line); color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .stamp { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-3); color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--s3-text-sm); line-height: var(--s3-text-sm-line); }
  .note { padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); border: var(--border-thin) dashed var(--border-control); border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-size: var(--s3-text-sm); line-height: var(--s3-text-sm-line); }

  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, var(--s3-card-min)), 1fr)); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .card-title { font-size: var(--display-card-size); line-height: 28px; font-weight: 650; }
  .card-text { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--s3-text-sm); line-height: var(--s3-text-sm-line); }
  .card-wps { margin-top: auto; color: var(--text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--s3-text-xs); line-height: var(--s3-text-xs-line); }
  .plan-note { margin-top: var(--space-6); max-width: var(--prose-max); color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--s3-text-sm); line-height: var(--s3-text-sm-line); }

  .later { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, var(--s3-card-min)), 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); counter-reset: later; }
  .later li { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); border: var(--border-thin) dashed var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--radius-md); color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .follow { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .follow a { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: var(--space-6); }
</style>
